# Conventions

See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Plugin

- App id `eduardkolotushin-forecast-app`
- Nested panel id `eduardkolotushin-forecast-panel`
- Nested datasource id `eduardkolotushin-forecast-datasource`
- Backend executable `gpx_forecast` (app process and a copy under `forecast-datasource/`)
- Go 1.26+

## API

- `POST /forecast` returns new points and optional `lower`/`upper`; do not mutate inputs
- `cacheKey` / `needTrain` / `retrain` skip the train query when a snapshot exists
- Panel forecasts each numeric series independently
- Panel `showInterval` gates `level`; training uses a from/to query, not the visible range; forecast uses a from/to window (`ForecastRange`)
- Train rewrite is type-keyed in the overlay frontend (Prom / OpenSearch / Postgres / Druid); `pkg/` has no Prom/OS/PG **datasource** clients (pgx snapshot store is allowed)
- Snapshot DSN: `FORECAST_STORE_*` (Grafana 12.4+ does not forward host env by default), then the `GF_PLUGIN_*` variables of this process's own `[plugin.<id>]` section — the id-qualified `GF_PLUGIN_EDUARDKOLOTUSHIN_FORECAST_APP_*` / `GF_PLUGIN_EDUARDKOLOTUSHIN_FORECAST_DATASOURCE_*` first, then the id-less `GF_PLUGIN_<KEY>` Grafana 13 exports (`[plugin.<id>] store_host` → `GF_PLUGIN_STORE_HOST`) — then GrafanaCfg, then jsonData; CI merges `conf/forecast.ini.template` (app and datasource plugin sections)
- Datasource `QueryData` Restores by `cacheKey` and emits forecast / lower / upper; miss is an error (overlay trains). Do not query other datasources from `pkg/`
- Overlay Mixed: cacheKey and train use metric targets only; Forecast datasource frames are not fitted or plotted
- Forecast query editor does not auto-fill; Copy source from query A is opt-in for `sourceTargets` only
- Overlay options New alert rule builds the rule from panel state: the metric queries copied and one Forecast query synthesized (fit options, chosen `seriesName` / `seriesLabels` / `sourceTargets`, the overlay's `cacheKey`), both over `now - <Alert lookback> … now`, with two Reduce(`last`) nodes, a Math percent deviation, and a Threshold on it as the condition; `Alert series` is offered only when the panel has more than one series (with a `Select a series` placeholder until one is picked), and a metric row whose series carry no labels is named by the synthesized `__name__` where Grafana provides one and otherwise by a `sql`-expression condition that selects the series and computes the deviation; only a row nothing can name answers a reason; do not ship rules
- Cap `POST /forecast` / `QueryData` body and train length (`MAX_TRAIN_POINTS`); bound concurrent Fit / ForecastRange; 413/429 instead of unbounded queues. Overlay: max in-flight loads is a panel option (default 1); sequential series POSTs; no tight retry
- Pre-size Go slices to the request/window length

## Quality

- Table-driven tests next to the resource handler and `QueryData` (including oversize / busy load limits)
- Table-driven frontend tests next to train rewrite, extract, cache fingerprint, mixed frames, forecast-query `cacheKey`, overlay New alert rule defaults, and overlay load limits
- No drive-by refactors
- Keep Grafana scaffold files under `.config/` unless a plugin-tools upgrade requires it
